; Run on the segments last first, five cards a segment in (kind, wf, cls9, after, imm), three out: nextk (the
; segment after: 0 a pause, 1 a vowel, 2 a consonant), pfw (this word comes right before a pause) and, for a vowel,
; p1, Klatt's rule 9 factor in hundredths: the class of the first obstruent after it in its word (cls9: 160 a
; voiced fricative or JH, 120 B D G, 70 P T K), else of the first consonant (85 an unstressed nasal, else 100),
; else 120 if it is the word's last vowel and 100 if not. A nasal is stressed when a stressed vowel of its word
; comes right after it (imm). The consonants after the vowel are seen first, kept as runc and runo.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            rec     INP   kind     03-09: a segment
  04                    INP   wf
  05                    INP   cls
  06                    INP   after
  07                    INP   imm
  08                    CLA   z
  09                    STO   p1
  10                    CLA   kind     10-30: a vowel's p1: runo, else runc, else 120 - 20 after
  11                    SUB   n2
  12                    TAC   vowel
  13                    JMP   out
  14            vowel   CLA   runo
  15                    SUB   00
  16                    TAC   nob
  17                    CLA   runo
  18                    JMP   setp
  19            nob     CLA   runc
  20                    SUB   00
  21                    TAC   noc
  22                    CLA   runc
  23                    JMP   setp
  24            noc     CLA   after
  25                    SFT   10
  26                    STO   x
  27                    CLA   c120
  28                    SUB   x
  29                    SUB   x
  30            setp    STO   p1
  31            out     OUT   nextk    31-33: what lies ahead
  32                    OUT   pfw
  33                    OUT   p1
  34                    CLA   kind     34-69: this segment is ahead now
  35                    SUB   c8
  36                    TAC   sound
  37                    CLA   z        a pause: nothing ahead in a word, and a pause next
  38                    STO   nextk
  39                    CLA   00
  40                    STO   pfw
  41                    JMP   runs
  42            sound   CLA   kind
  43                    SUB   n2
  44                    TAC   vow
  45                    SUB   00
  46                    TAC   cons
  47                    SUB   00
  48                    TAC   nas
  49                    SUB   n3
  50                    TAC   obs
  51                    JMP   cons
  52            nas     CLA   imm
  53                    SUB   00
  54                    TAC   cons
  55                    CLA   c100
  56                    STO   cls
  57                    JMP   cons
  58            obs     CLA   cls
  59                    STO   runo
  60            cons    CLA   cls
  61                    STO   runc
  62                    CLA   n2
  63                    STO   nextk
  64                    JMP   word
  65            vow     CLA   00
  66                    STO   nextk
  67                    CLA   z
  68                    STO   runc
  69                    STO   runo
  70            word    CLA   wf       70-78: at a word's start nothing of this word is ahead
  71                    SUB   00
  72                    TAC   rec
  73                    CLA   z
  74                    STO   pfw
  75            runs    CLA   z
  76                    STO   runc
  77                    STO   runo
  78                    JMP   rec
  80            kind    DATA  0
  81            wf      DATA  0
  82            cls     DATA  0
  83            after   DATA  0
  84            imm     DATA  0
  85            p1      DATA  0
  86            nextk   DATA  0
  87            pfw     DATA  0
  88            runc    DATA  0
  89            runo    DATA  0
  90            x       DATA  0
  91            z       DATA  0
  92            c8      DATA  8
  93            n2      DATA  2
  94            n3      DATA  3
  95            c100    DATA  100
  96            c120    DATA  120
